-- Corvus universal loader: picks the hub for the current game and keeps a live dashboard in Discord.
-- The dashboard is two webhook messages that are edited, never re-posted:
--   StatsMessage (top): overview with trends and a 24 hour chart, every game with a share chart.
--   StatsData (below): players online, executors, the last 7 days and records. Its embeds also carry the whole
--   dashboard state as base64 in their hidden title/author links, so nothing technical is ever visible.
-- Charts are images from QuickChart (only totals are sent). Players with Anonymous Mode on (Info tab) show as
-- "Anonymous". Unique and online players are counted with bitmaps of hashed user ids, so the stored state stays
-- small no matter how many people play.
-- Filled in by tools/github_upload.py when the loader is uploaded (raw URL of the repo that holds the hubs).
